# Rust crypto-rs — generated Android native libs + UniFFI Kotlin bindings
/mobile/src/main/jniLibs/
/mobile/build/generated/source/uniffi/
/crypto-rs/target/
# The .so provenance manifest describes those untracked binaries, so it cannot be
# a source file: a committed copy only ever describes whichever machine last ran
# build-android.sh. That is how the first public snapshot came to ship a manifest
# naming a private -dirty commit (audit 2026-08-28, F-04). It is regenerated on
# every build and published as an artifact of the release run, next to the .so.
/crypto-rs/PROVENANCE.txt
# cargo-mutants run output (mutation-testing reports) — regenerated, not tracked
/crypto-rs/mutants.out/
/crypto-rs/mutants.out.old/
java_pid18084.hprof
/mobile/release/

